# SS-22 - Real-market learning demonstrations
Workstream ID: SS-22
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/22
Status: DONE
Milestone: M2
Dependencies: SS-03, SS-05, SS-06, SS-20, SS-21

## Purpose
Let humans inspect an algorithm applying to actual observed market prices while
learning it, without selecting only winners or implying guaranteed profitability.

## Tasks
- [x] Add an independent real-history picker from each of 27 technical lessons.
- [x] Reuse causal simulation, costs and captured stock/strategy assumptions.
- [x] Show revealed indicator values, decision/fill distinction and next-event navigation.
- [x] Add bounded book history exercises and isolated real-company worksheets.
- [x] Verify all lesson routes, causal views, failures and actual network/native use.
- [x] Document applicability, limitations and completion evidence.

## Acceptance criteria
- Every implemented technical rule has a learning demo with actual history,
  graphical rule measurements, dated decisions/trades and marked profit/loss.
- No stock/interval is silently swapped for a winner; losing/no-signal outcomes persist.
- Warmup, next-open execution, missing sessions, costs and adjusted units remain explicit.
- Existing Explore studies and original workbook inputs are not overwritten.
- Applicable book exercises separate actual prices, current facts and assumptions;
  unsupported/qualitative concepts do not gain fabricated trading signals.
- Owned requests and playback close safely without user-window control.

## Completion evidence
- Full offline suite: 322 passed, 4 opt-in live cases skipped, normal exit.
  Ruff lint/format, strict mypy and Git whitespace checks passed.
- Actual ICICIBANK snapshot: 496 observations, 2024-11-21 through 2026-11-20.
  Owned native checks exercised all 27 learning lessons, four book history
  exercises and a real current-company fetch/calculation with bank guards.
- Inspected actual rule/explanation, equal-money and company worksheet views
  at 1366x768. Final rule replay uses two persistent axes without stale labels.
- Causal-prefix, independent-state, event-navigation, failure and lifecycle
  regressions pass. Technical acceptance is not human approval or a profit proof.
- Published v0.3.0 remains unchanged and does not contain these source additions.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-21: Traced existing lessons, studies and replay. Reused rule guides and
  execution rather than introducing a competing set of trading formulas.
- 2026-11-21: Completed source-native demonstrations and guide. Preserved
  losing/no-signal outcomes; no winner search, user-window control or new EXE.
  Corrected overlapping replay-axis labels by retaining the rule chart's axes.
